This extension adds METAL GEAR SOLID V: THE PHANTOM PAIN modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]SnakeBite automatically installed.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Snakebite Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "SnakeBite Installer.exe" file.[/*]
[*]MGSVFix mods with a "mgsvfix.asi" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "master" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]SnakeBite mods with a ".mgsv" or ".MGSVPreset" file install to the "SnakeBite_Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Deploying only places .mgsv files in the "SnakeBite_Mods" folder. SnakeBite still has to install them into the game archives before they do anything in game.[/*]
[*]The "Install Mods with SnakeBite" button on the Mods toolbar does that for you, as does the "Sync" button on the notification shown after deploying. It installs everything Vortex has deployed, removes the mods it previously installed that Vortex no longer has, and reports anything it had to skip.[/*]
[*]Mods you installed yourself in SnakeBite are reported after a sync but are never removed on their own. The results dialog has a button to remove them if you want them gone.[/*]
[*]A sync repacks the game archives, so it can take a while. Turning off the automatic preset backup in SnakeBite's own settings makes it noticeably faster, at the cost of SnakeBite's revert option.[/*]
[*]"Restore Original Game Files" on the Mods toolbar puts the game back the way it was before any mod was installed. That removes every mod, including any installed outside Vortex, and SnakeBite runs its setup wizard the next time it is started.[/*]
[*]Settings > Mods has two switches, both off by default: one runs the sync automatically after every deployment, the other has SnakeBite remove the mods from the game when you purge.[/*]
[*]Purging removes the deployed files but not the mods already inside the game archives, so a warning appears afterwards if any are still installed, with a button to restore the original game files.[/*]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically downloads and installs [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/metalgearsolidvtpp/mods/106]SnakeBite Mod Manager[/url][/b]. Needed to install most mods.[/*]
[*].mgsv mods are install to "SnakeBite_Mods" folder.  You add files to SB manually. The installer provides file selection when more than one .mgsv file are included with a mod.[/*]
[*]Offers to download [url=https://codeberg.org/Lyall/MGSVFix]MGSVFix[/url] for the user from codeberg via a notification.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for METAL GEAR SOLID V: THE PHANTOM PAIN mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Snakebite Mod Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "SnakeBite Installer.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

MGSVFix:

Recognised when the archive contains a "mgsvfix.asi" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── master\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "master" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

SnakeBite Mod (.mgsv):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".mgsv" or ".MGSVPreset" file.

  Installs to: "SnakeBite_Mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
